{"tool_name":"plm_blast","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"plm_blast","home":"https://toolkit.tuebingen.mpg.de/tools/plmblast","license":"MIT","summary":"Distant homology detection based on direct comparison of sequence representations from protein language models.","addition_date":"2024-03-18T17:01:40.456422Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:08:15.145145Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:plm_blast","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"stanislaw.dunin-horkawicz@tuebingen.mpg.de","name":"Stanislaw Dunin-Horkawicz","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4581-1558","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Global alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0496"},{"term":"Local alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0495"},{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"},{"term":"Structure classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2996"},{"term":"Structure-based sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0294"}]}],"name":"pLM-BLAST","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btad579","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The detection of homology through sequence comparison is a typical first step in the study of protein function and evolution. In this work, we explore the applicability of protein language models to this task. Results: We introduce pLM-BLAST, a tool inspired by BLAST, that detects distant homology by comparing single-sequence representations (embeddings) derived from a protein language model, ProtT5. Our benchmarks reveal that pLM-BLAST maintains a level of accuracy on par with HHsearch for both highly similar sequences (with >50% identity) and markedly divergent sequences (with <30% identity), while being significantly faster. Additionally, pLM-BLAST stands out among other embedding-based tools due to its ability to compute local alignments. We show that these local alignments, produced by pLM-BLAST, often connect highly divergent proteins, thereby highlighting its potential to uncover previously undiscovered homologous relationships and improve protein annotation.","authors":[{"name":"Alva V."},{"name":"Dunin-Horkawicz S."},{"name":"Kaminski K."},{"name":"Ludwiczak J."},{"name":"Pawlicki K."}],"citationCount":13,"date":"2023-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"pLM-BLAST: distant homology detection based on direct comparison of sequence representations from protein language models"},"pmcid":"PMC10576641","pmid":"37725369"}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"Evolutionary biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3299"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"pLM-BLAST","home":"https://bio.tools/plm_blast","license":"MIT","summary":"Distant homology detection based on direct comparison of sequence representations from protein language models.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:plm_blast/cmd/toolkit.tuebingen.mpg.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":41,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":12,"year":"2026"},{"count":13,"year":"2024"},{"count":15,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btad579","pmcid":"PMC10576641","pmid":"37725369","ref_count":33,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"1970"},{"count":1,"year":"1992"},{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"